<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Filippo Maria Visconti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1392">1392</a>–<a href="/years/1447">1447</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Filippo Maria Visconti (1392–1447) was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 1412, the last of the Visconti line. He rebuilt the state of his father, Gian Galeazzo, after its collapse and waged long wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, relying on condottieri such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-sforza">Francesco Sforza</a>, to whom he married his only child, the illegitimate Bianca Maria. After his death without a legitimate heir, Milan briefly became the Golden Ambrosian Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/filippo-maria-visconti.jpg" alt="Filippo Maria Visconti" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pisanello · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pisanello_-_Codex_Vallardi_2484.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under <b>Filippo Maria Visconti</b> (r. 1412–1447) captains such as Francesco Bussone da Carmagnola and Niccolò Piccinino reconquered much of Lombardy, but Carmagnola later served Venice and defeated Milan at the Battle of Maclodio in 1427; Venice gained Brescia and Bergamo, and its frontier stayed on the Adda River…</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Duchy of Milan · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>When Duke <b>Filippo Maria Visconti</b> died without a male heir in August 1447, a group of Milanese nobles and lawyers proclaimed a republic named after the city's patron saint Ambrose.</blockquote><a href="/state/golden-ambrosian-republic">Golden Ambrosian Republic</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.47,9.19&amp;year=1427" aria-label="Milan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4768 560 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Filippo Maria Visconti"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5218 830h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=45.47,9.19&amp;year=1427">What was here in 1427? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
